{"term":"lively","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:4b7cc8ee3cc09a9aa5","definition":"Full of life; energetic, vivacious.","example":"But wherefore comes old Manoa in such haſt, / With youthful ſteps? much livelier then e're while / He ſeems.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["high-spirited"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["livelily","liveliness","lively as a grig","livened","look lively","overlively","unlively"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lively#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6a992afdfd1d889c87","definition":"Bright, glowing, vivid; strong, vigorous.","example":"The colours of the prism are manifestly more full, intense, and lively that those of natural bodies.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["intense","smart"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["livelily","liveliness","lively as a grig","livened","look lively","overlively","unlively"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lively#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3ee9dc975f18b6a135","definition":"Endowed with or manifesting life; living.","example":"c. 1600, Philemon Holland\nchaplets of gold and silver resembling lively flowers and leaves","pos":"adj","synonyms":["extant"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic","wordFamily":["livelily","liveliness","lively as a grig","livened","look lively","overlively","unlively"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lively#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2d4e2479772b07644a","definition":"Representing life; lifelike.","example":"I spied the lively picture of my father.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["lifey","limned","naturalistic"],"antonyms":[],"colloca